Honeybee local security patch, September 18, 2026

Derived from @libp2p/peer-store 11.2.7, libp2p/js-libp2p contributors.
Upstream declares Apache-2.0 OR MIT; this copy is distributed under Apache-2.0.
All existing upstream notices and package metadata are retained.

Modification: reject a PeerRecord whose payload peer ID differs from the peer
ID derived from the verified envelope public key, before any store read/write.
The same guard is added to the TypeScript source and exported JavaScript.
Local version: 11.2.7-honeybee.1. This is not an upstream release.

Motivation: npm audit's GHSA-vrf4-mx87-p53w report, plus inspection and a local
synthetic-peer regression of the installed implementation. This preserves the
existing libp2p 2 / peer-store 11 interfaces instead of forcing peer-store 12.
The npm advisory may still flag the upstream version family; do not describe
this as a clean advisory audit or an independently audited dependency.

The package export uses dist/src/index.js. The unused standalone minified bundle
and nested node_modules were not copied. Original source maps are retained as
upstream reference, not regenerated mapping evidence for the inserted guard.
Upstream development dependencies were omitted from the local runtime package
so directory installation does not pull unrelated build/test tools into the app.

Reference: https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-vrf4-mx87-p53w
